# Agent architecture — backend + SDK split

## Rule

**100% of agent business logic** lives in `apps/api/src/agents/<agentId>/`:

- Agent definitions (`agent.ts`, step executors, prompts)
- Schemas and output normalization
- `learning/feedback-handler.ts` (mandatory per agent)
- Ports (`CutsRunDeps`, etc.) and Nest adapters that wire Prisma, storage, Trigger

**`packages/agent-ia-sdk`** owns **IA infrastructure only**:

- `ia/` — STT, LLM, image, embedding, RAG (providers + runtime)
- `agents/` — workflow **kernel** (execute-run, AgentBuilder, generic steps like `createLlmCallStep`)

The SDK must **not** contain agent-specific business logic (no `cuts` steps, prompts, or schemas).

## Forbidden in apps/api

- Duplicate IA provider adapters (AssemblyAI, OpenRouter, Gemini) — use `sdk.ia.*` only
- `ai-runtime/` or inline LLM/STT calls outside the SDK

## Allowed in apps/api (thin shell)

- HTTP controllers (`POST /api/agents/:agentId/run`, review, SSE)
- Registry / loader (`agent-catalog.ts`)
- Adapters: Prisma run store, credits, storage, event publishers, `buildCutsRunDeps`
- `WorkflowEngineService` orchestration (inline vs Trigger.dev)

## Required per agent (apps/api)

```
apps/api/src/agents/<agentId>/
  agent.ts
  schemas/
  prompts/
  steps/
  learning/feedback-handler.ts   ← mandatory
  ports/                           ← deps interface + adapter wiring
```

## Agent IDs (canonical)

Default: `research`, `cuts`, `video_editor`  
Marketplace: `planning`, `script`, `thumbnail`, `distribution`

## When adding an agent

1. Implement business logic in `apps/api/src/agents/<agentId>/`
2. Register in `agent-catalog.ts`
3. Wire deps adapter + permission keys in authz
4. Use `@company-os/agent-ia-sdk` for all `ia.*` calls
5. Doc in `docs/agents/<agentId>/README.md`

Never put agent-specific workflow logic in `packages/agent-ia-sdk`.
